{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he built there an altar.</b> And adjacent to it is 'וְתָמָת דְּבוֹרָה,' and the Ramban raised the difficulty: what is the relevance of the death of Deborah between these two verses? And I say that this is like what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Mo'ed Katan 28a) — why is the death of Miriam juxtaposed to the section of the red heifer? To tell you: just as the heifer atones, so the death of the righteous atones. So too here, for it speaks of the death of Rebekah and Deborah, as they derived from the verse 'אַלּוֹן בָּכוּת,' and Jacob indicated that their death is an altar of atonement — therefore he built an altar in the place where their death was made known to him. 'וַיְבָרֶךְ אֹתוֹ אֱלֹהִים' (Genesis 35:9) — this is the blessing of mourners, just as He blessed Isaac after his mother's death. And what is stated, 'וַתִּקָּבֵר מִתַּחַת לְבֵית אֵל' (Genesis 35:8) — this hints that he eulogized her as fitting, for Beit El was on the mountain, and had he not eulogized her the mountain would have heaved against them, as they expounded regarding Mount Ga'ash (Shabbat 105b). And Scripture further informs us that he eulogized more than was fitting, for it is stated: 'מִתַּחַת לְבֵית אֵל תַּחַת הָאַלּוֹן' — what is 'מִתַּחַת'? Rather, he began underneath the city, and from there he prolonged the eulogy until underneath the oak. And this is the indication of the mem of 'מִתַּחַת,' that he was transported from place to place and eulogized her in several places. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Mo'ed Katan 27b): whoever is overly pained over one deceased more than is fitting — he is weeping over another deceased. Therefore this place was called 'אַלּוֹן בָּכוּת' — weeping for another, for there the death of Rebekah his mother was made known to him, or as an allusion to the death of Rachel, which was also near this place."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:06.666381932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}